_explanation":"Principle: A fresher resume should present truthful evidence of communication, responsibility, tools, projects and availability in a format recruiters can scan quickly. Example: Turn college-event coordination into evidence of handling enquiries, maintaining records and resolving schedule conflicts without calling it professional support experience. Workplace method: Match the role, write a factual summary, convert education and activities into evidence, quantify only verified results, proofread and prepare documents. Example: Use One-page resume, job-description match and document checklist and retain evidence of the result. Quality and interview check: Verify the outcome, explain trade-offs and avoid: Adding false experience, generic objectives, skill ratings without evidence or unnecessary personal information. Example: Present two transferable skills from college or part-time experience without exaggerating them.","key_terms":[{"term":"Resume Writing","definition":"A practical capability used in resume and job preparation work.","example":"Turn college-event coordination into evidence of handling enquiries, maintaining records and resolving schedule conflicts without calling it professional support experience."},{"term":"Job Readiness","definition":"A practical capability used in resume and job preparation work.","example":"Turn college-event coordination into evidence of handling enquiries, maintaining records and resolving schedule conflicts without calling it professional support experience."}]},"principles":{"rules":[{"rule_number":1,"title":"Principle","explanation":"A fresher resume should present truthful evidence of communication, responsibility, tools, projects and availability in a format recruiters can scan quickly.","why_it_works":"Example: Turn college-event coordination into evidence of handling enquiries, maintaining records and resolving schedule conflicts without calling it professional support experience.","exception":null},{"rul