necessary personal information."},"worked_examples":[{"example_number":1,"title":"Guided practice","difficulty":"Foundation to applied","question_or_scenario":"Practise this workflow: Match the role, write a factual summary, convert education and activities into evidence, quantify only verified results, proofread and prepare documents.","given_information":["Resume Writing","Job Readiness"],"reasoning_steps":[{"step_number":1,"explanation":"Review the apply requirements and define the expected result."},{"step_number":2,"explanation":"Turn college-event coordination into evidence of handling enquiries, maintaining records and resolving schedule conflicts without calling it professional support experience."},{"step_number":3,"explanation":"Validate the outcome. Avoid this common mistake: Adding false experience, generic objectives, skill ratings without evidence or unnecessary personal information."}],"final_answer":"Match the role, write a factual summary, convert education and activities into evidence, quantify only verified results, proofread and prepare documents.","why_the_answer_is_correct":"The result follows the defined process, covers the required elements and includes a validation step.","learning_takeaway":"Avoid this common mistake: Adding false experience, generic objectives, skill ratings without evidence or unnecessary personal information."}],"usage_comparisons":[],"common_mistakes":[{"mistake_number":1,"title":"Acting before understanding","incorrect_approach":"Starting immediately without confirming scope, inputs and success criteria.","why_students_make_it":"Speed can feel more important than process discipline.","why_it_is_wrong":"An incomplete process creates unreliable results and avoidable rework.","correction":"Define the outcome, complete the workflow, and validate it once.","prevention_tip":"Avoid this common mistake: Adding false experience, generic objectives, skill ratings without evidence or unnecessary personal information."}],"memory_s