ns for HR, voice, grammar, chat and email rounds. The work should be reproducible and reviewed against a clear outcome.","key_points":["Interview Readiness","Voice Screening","Written Assessment","Avoid this common mistake: Reciting a generic script, claiming perfect communication, criticising customers or agreeing to shifts you cannot work."],"one_minute_revision":"Interview Preparation: Practical Workflow: Identify what is evaluated, choose a concise structure, give a truthful example, connect it to the role and practise variations for HR, voice, grammar, chat and email rounds. The work should be reproducible and reviewed against a clear outcome.","final_checklist":["I can explain the concept.","I can complete the activity.","I can validate and present the result."]},"quality_metadata":{"content_origin":"taksh_authored","review_status":"approved","copyright_review_status":"original","prompt_version":"deterministic-v2","generated_by":"taksh","sections_not_applicable":[]}}'::jsonb,content_version=content_version+1,reviewed_at=now(),approved_at=now(),published_at=now(),skill_tags=array['Interview Readiness','Voice Screening','Written Assessment']::text[],updated_at=now()
